WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:08.670
the midterms are first and foremost
about Congress and they can make or

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:12.540
break a president's agenda
Republican control of both the House of

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:17.910
Representatives and the Senate has made
Trump's life relatively easy so far but

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:22.619
if Democrats flip one or even both
houses the good times may be over the

00:00:22.619 --> 00:00:27.650
entire house all 435 seats are up for
election and they are every two years

00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:33.899
Republicans currently hold 235 to
Democrats 193 seats that's a lot of

00:00:33.899 --> 00:00:38.070
distance to the 218 majority mark but
Democrats hope that the slew of

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:42.180
Republicans leaving their seats this
year along with enough anti-trump fury

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:47.250
among voters will deliver them the house
so all eyes are on the 30 or so toss-ups

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:52.010
race is that polling data have is too
close to call on the Senate side

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:57.539
Republicans rule with the slimmest of
majorities 51 of 100 seats sounds like

00:00:57.539 --> 00:01:02.760
good news for Democrats but only 35
seats of those are up for election most

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:08.159
26 are ones Democrats and independents
allied with them need to defend that

00:01:08.159 --> 00:01:12.210
makes victory harder polling data
suggests maybe just six seats in all our

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:17.040
toss ups as the minority party Democrats
have been limited in effectively

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:21.509
resisting Trump but what if they win in
both the House and Senate they could

00:01:21.509 --> 00:01:26.040
block his agenda and introduce their own
they could investigate the myriad

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:31.049
allegations of abuse and misconduct
facing Trump in the Senate Democrats

00:01:31.049 --> 00:01:35.490
could reject Trump appointees up for
important positions and they could

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:39.960
impeach a long and fraught process that
starts in the house and ends in the

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:44.970
Senate Democrats have history on their
side as the president's party usually

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:49.500
suffers in the midterms whether that
trend stays true won't be clear until

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:53.740
ballots are in
you

